<title>AUSTRIA: Kuwait says in no hurry to claim extra OPEC quota.</title>
<headline>Kuwait says in no hurry to claim extra OPEC quota.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kuwaiti oil minister Isa al-Mazeedi said he was prepared not to push in the near future for any extra OPEC quota despite over-production from the large majority of OPEC producers.</p>
<p>&quot;Probably at the moment we are sacrificing but because of our strong desire to maintain prices that is why we are restricting ourselves,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Kuwait has a long standing claim to an extra 200,000 barrels per day on top of its 2 million bpd quota which it established in a series of steps following its return to the market after the 1990-1991 Gulf War.</p>
<p>&quot;Right now we are not talking about any increment because we are trying to maintain the level of OPEC production and the level of the oil market,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
